Let two settings of TAL-SH, which are compile-time constants, be changed from
the environment. Both are read once, when TAL-SH starts. Without the
variables TAL-SH behaves as before.

TALSH_GFLOP_THRESH_GPU=<GFlop>
    A contraction runs on a GPU only if its size is above this threshold.
    The built-in value is 4. With 0 every contraction runs on a GPU.

TALSH_GPU_BUFFER_MB=<MiB>
    Upper limit of the memory that TAL-SH reserves on each GPU. The built-in
    behavior is to reserve 90 % of the free memory of every visible GPU.

For the ExaTensor revision that ExaTN c528f7e pins (e9efb95). Apply in the
submodule tpls/ExaTensor of the ExaTN source tree:

    git -C tpls/ExaTensor apply /path/to/exatensor.patch

